[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-15717"] :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{8}{3}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{3x}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C,$ we can always write $C=\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K$ where $K$ is some other positive constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$ term, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{3x}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|x|).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885/selection/12c8c5f7b8a9756216ffaaa91a53915e68fe209986c9f64c4f1f572f773a8dc0" :answer/id #uuid "fe940d4c-1be7-5233-beb3-e7ec924193be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}{x}^{4/3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885/selection/08b174c071735a3ddda3aa2d3de55b679d6b4be4674af92d7372ac54c4db5a4f" :answer/id #uuid "9cdd1613-c193-5531-b4b3-85a2b86f8aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}{x}^{5/3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885/selection/1c1a7a11a2d027ccd9355369f2dc20c4827723072feae544ea2c668b9251da50" :answer/id #uuid "736449a4-ac71-5767-b3fc-e14d9a921eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}{x}^{11/3}+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885/selection/44769e57c2aa9b0d2263032172b0dcf1489e1b2586d0454da9f136ea3fd0f05b" :answer/id #uuid "10662836-c250-5b2b-ac39-d78242a32aec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}{x}^{7/3}+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885/selection/aee0c7bceefa2d967b205342598cdea73ffd2eba6256f65d266e029550d9bae0" :answer/id #uuid "934471f6-fc89-51ea-b95d-ba62554e17f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5/3}+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0da6736-bbca-5bea-9f9b-514f7721c773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29885/selection/aee0c7bceefa2d967b205342598cdea73ffd2eba6256f65d266e029550d9bae0" :answer-field/choices ["q-29885/selection/12c8c5f7b8a9756216ffaaa91a53915e68fe209986c9f64c4f1f572f773a8dc0" "q-29885/selection/08b174c071735a3ddda3aa2d3de55b679d6b4be4674af92d7372ac54c4db5a4f" "q-29885/selection/1c1a7a11a2d027ccd9355369f2dc20c4827723072feae544ea2c668b9251da50" "q-29885/selection/44769e57c2aa9b0d2263032172b0dcf1489e1b2586d0454da9f136ea3fd0f05b" "q-29885/selection/aee0c7bceefa2d967b205342598cdea73ffd2eba6256f65d266e029550d9bae0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29885" :question/id #uuid "a1fd3399-f36e-569b-89f9-d06cadb048a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-29885" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{2/3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{x})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and get\n\n$$\n\\int ({x}^{2/3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{x})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, using the power rule in the first term, and taking out the coefficient in the second term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{2/3+1}}{\\frac{2}{3}+1}+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5/3}+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29885/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29885"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369/selection/37472eef8c1e8a5cf30dec43d75f6b51e4c53ef70a36dd5f400c094af5016998" :answer/id #uuid "18a0496a-ccc4-5097-9dc8-841e78b4bbf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369/selection/48b06aba9b7e02ac4139a757046588a159885e50e6e79a97fb4d9d6d7016cc0d" :answer/id #uuid "559d13df-72d2-5cda-b5d2-af330986e8a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369/selection/0415c3a16c094017d4f6f1c883b934385f8202662d090027cd2a7f63101d658a" :answer/id #uuid "8aa30e16-fb89-5f63-b2fd-d91407ee49f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|}{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369/selection/d1e10b56a8d9f3a0198ace936139d9aa05620792adc201348f59625016fabaf2" :answer/id #uuid "dc97a57e-9fd5-53b8-8e0a-bb353da266a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369/selection/921f2d7ba2a753f4f1cbac0f37ed6d00a670203c0f99c717aa738c3c83af2020" :answer/id #uuid "e908a26f-a0e2-54a0-9278-1432dd5d812e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f0d744-84b4-51ea-a1c9-cc96b8478494" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103369/selection/48b06aba9b7e02ac4139a757046588a159885e50e6e79a97fb4d9d6d7016cc0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-103369/selection/37472eef8c1e8a5cf30dec43d75f6b51e4c53ef70a36dd5f400c094af5016998" "q-103369/selection/48b06aba9b7e02ac4139a757046588a159885e50e6e79a97fb4d9d6d7016cc0d" "q-103369/selection/0415c3a16c094017d4f6f1c883b934385f8202662d090027cd2a7f63101d658a" "q-103369/selection/d1e10b56a8d9f3a0198ace936139d9aa05620792adc201348f59625016fabaf2" "q-103369/selection/921f2d7ba2a753f4f1cbac0f37ed6d00a670203c0f99c717aa738c3c83af2020"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103369" :question/id #uuid "8fc6231a-b956-5ba4-98e6-075eb6f03f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103369" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{5}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $5$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103369/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf98ee24-7774-5674-8a1e-63f4f6d225c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593/selection/e3dcbf32d08f57cbced1206ee43a408a1a8ad29626a1735b545999f7c39166da" :answer/id #uuid "a7408c64-3fb6-5a07-9cd4-7f0ab853ebce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593/selection/d667160d1ef3cf419f525954c74012510c31d0ed2eb865fe628d9cea1fa55dc8" :answer/id #uuid "1fce1b83-deb1-5ab4-a42c-c41a40c94396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593/selection/3331ab23bcaf1d95706db54ca50009fe849182c6ee7c09b976161aaed7f4d1f2" :answer/id #uuid "7668c788-98b3-51e2-bd1a-52cae21b39b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5/2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593/selection/e116a850acbff704e4ef3b1c3725f25d81a70e5abfa6b998a452be2456987663" :answer/id #uuid "4be80ff3-1b3b-5e71-b2e9-1371b757622e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{5/2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593/selection/2df4083769f15add821bd26c2dff8f218d3a359dfd4d28d7e1baec99c95c69ca" :answer/id #uuid "f2d6fe6f-8eae-567d-9dea-90b7d5157218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f7f4c6f-37c5-5504-b65e-fb3646a79d73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103593/selection/e3dcbf32d08f57cbced1206ee43a408a1a8ad29626a1735b545999f7c39166da" :answer-field/choices ["q-103593/selection/e3dcbf32d08f57cbced1206ee43a408a1a8ad29626a1735b545999f7c39166da" "q-103593/selection/d667160d1ef3cf419f525954c74012510c31d0ed2eb865fe628d9cea1fa55dc8" "q-103593/selection/3331ab23bcaf1d95706db54ca50009fe849182c6ee7c09b976161aaed7f4d1f2" "q-103593/selection/e116a850acbff704e4ef3b1c3725f25d81a70e5abfa6b998a452be2456987663" "q-103593/selection/2df4083769f15add821bd26c2dff8f218d3a359dfd4d28d7e1baec99c95c69ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103593" :question/id #uuid "f6168e0f-95d3-5bb7-aa52-ddc60f3cb1e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103593" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and get\n\n$$\n\\int ({x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, using the power rule in the first term, and taking out the coefficient in the second term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2+1}}{\\frac{3}{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103593/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605/selection/4d5167e7803755e0e48603ecb1e235086b2fd088a4d5aaa9c145920f891699de" :answer/id #uuid "9c1f87c6-0ec1-5d29-9b42-93b4b1eedba3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|x|)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605/selection/8eff74a3f919d0665c41d339f8a1771666396e77e2efaf65ab762b090d2628d6" :answer/id #uuid "f230377c-ba24-53bb-a49a-77160503441d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|x|)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605/selection/c92069de9469d7a890f1498a3b7c40dd8d16ec09fc3459a84f7f132ea4e70940" :answer/id #uuid "5cfa26b9-e523-5a59-af88-a097ff241327" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|x|)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605/selection/808cc9a8f7c44016f3981805c1b51786fdd968c211831dd6229367bf02707362" :answer/id #uuid "1e0b6d48-31b3-57cc-ba54-4810982c2af7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(|x|+K)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605/selection/4cb14f65899ac587a74c7a28656f84ec0771c5e5b444aacfb9b9590f80988278" :answer/id #uuid "8a978206-6017-5bd1-8b0e-72c43b05fbae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|x|)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "82405685-59a1-5e2c-a847-3310686c49d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103605/selection/4cb14f65899ac587a74c7a28656f84ec0771c5e5b444aacfb9b9590f80988278" :answer-field/choices ["q-103605/selection/4d5167e7803755e0e48603ecb1e235086b2fd088a4d5aaa9c145920f891699de" "q-103605/selection/8eff74a3f919d0665c41d339f8a1771666396e77e2efaf65ab762b090d2628d6" "q-103605/selection/c92069de9469d7a890f1498a3b7c40dd8d16ec09fc3459a84f7f132ea4e70940" "q-103605/selection/808cc9a8f7c44016f3981805c1b51786fdd968c211831dd6229367bf02707362" "q-103605/selection/4cb14f65899ac587a74c7a28656f84ec0771c5e5b444aacfb9b9590f80988278"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103605" :question/id #uuid "de38dc2b-38ee-5deb-9b32-6e4c664420c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103605" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of $\\frac{2x-1}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "We separate the integrand into the sum of two fractions so that we can simplify each term. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x}{x}-\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C,$ we can always write $C=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡K$ where $K$ is some other positive constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$ term, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =2x-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡K) \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|x|).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103605/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df7dddc6-a4fd-5b1b-9b73-8528e5224ca9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103605"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
